have a matrix structure like this
Construct 1: 6 items
Construct 2: 9 items
Construct 3: 10 items
Construct 4; 7 items
Construct 5; 4 items
Construct 6: 10 items

Is there any general syntax for factor variance and error covariance and factor mean data in simsem? The documentation on simsem.org <http://simsem.org> is bit rigid in terms of varieties of example in context of asymmetrical matrices.

=================================================================================

==
Asymmetrical Matrix
=================================================================================

==

loadingVal <- matrix(0, 34, 6)
loadingVal[1:5, 1] <- c(1,0.6, 0.7,0.6,0.7)
loadingVal[6:11, 2] <- c(1,1.1, 0.9,0.9,0.7,0.8)
