Your first model makes the DV an exclusive indicator of the G factor (just like its other indicators) and forces it to be orthogonal to the S factors, while the second relaxes these restrictions. Does the first model fit well, or does it not? If it does not there may be bias in parameter estimates, which might induce a too-high R2.

